  "method": "Market-cap snapshot of the ten largest distinct US-exchange-listed companies in each of the ten requested sectors, using Stock Analysis sector tables fetched via authenticated Firecrawl CLI with --max-age 0. The obsolete /list/technology-stocks/ and /list/healthcare-stocks/ URLs returned 404; the working /stocks/sector/ pages are cited. Companies are taken in descending source market-cap order after excluding alternate securities and duplicate companies; rank is the resulting company rank, not necessarily the original table row number. Eligibility includes US-listed domestic and foreign common equities, ADRs/depositary shares, and REIT common equities, regardless of company domicile; it excludes ETFs, funds, preferred securities, debt, OTC-only securities, and non-US-exchange-only listings. All 100 selected tickers were corroborated against the source Nasdaq and NYSE stock lists (https://stockanalysis.com/list/nasdaq-stocks/ and https://stockanalysis.com/list/nyse-stocks/); SKHY, SPCX, and VMRK were additionally checked on their individual Stock Analysis company pages. A company appears once: use GOOGL rather than GOOG, BRK-B rather than BRK-A, PBR rather than PBR.A, and SO rather than SOMN. Skipping PBR.A brings PSX into Energy; skipping SOMN brings VST into Utilities. Symbols use Yahoo-compatible class notation (BRK.B becomes BRK-B). Sector assignments follow the Stock Analysis taxonomy described at https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/industry/, not an independently verified official GICS classification or a mixture of different vendors. Source Technology maps to requested IT / Technology; the other nine labels are capitalization-normalized equivalents of the source labels. Materials is intentionally omitted. Provider-specific assignments, such as AppLovin in Communication Services, are retained even when other taxonomies may assign a company differently. market_cap_usd is the source-reported company market capitalization, not the value of only the US-listed ADR float; displayed T/B/M/K values are converted to numeric USD without inventing precision beyond the rounded source display. The sector and exchange tables supply no explicit market-cap as-of timestamp, so sources.as_of is null. retrieved_at records completion of source collection in UTC, not an exchange timestamp, and fresh retrieval does not prove real-time quotes. Individual pages checked for SKHY, SPCX, and VMRK show an Oct 2, 2026 close; that date is not extrapolated to all sector-table valuations. This is a single-provider snapshot, not an independently reconciled market-wide ranking or a live data feed.",
